      "description": "Watch Celta Vigo vs Osasuna highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 27, 2026. The atmosphere was thick with anticipation as Celta Vigo hosted Osasuna in a high-stakes La Liga encounter on 2026-08-27. Both sides took to the pitch looking to establish early-season dominance, setting the stage for a match defined by tactical shifts and individual brilliance. Aspas Lights Up the First Half Celta Vigo began the match with intent, and it didn't take long for their talisman to make his mark. In the 14th minute, Iago Aspas received a sharp pass from Miguel Roman and unleashed a clinical left-footed strike from outside the penalty area. The ball flew past the keeper, sending the home crowd of 20,645 into raptures. For the remainder of the first half, Celta looked comfortable, while Osasuna struggled to find their rhythm, frequently caught offside as they tried to catch the hosts on the break. The Turning Point: VAR Intervention The complexion of the match changed entirely early in the second half. In the 51st minute, Marcos Alonso was involved in a serious foul that caught the referee's attention. Following a VAR review, the initial yellow card was upgraded to a red, leaving Celta Vigo with ten men. The tactical fallout was immediate; the goalscorer Iago Aspas was substituted for defender Carl Starfelt as the hosts scrambled to plug the hole in their backline. Osasuna Capitalize on the Advantage With a man advantage, Osasuna wasted no time in mounting a comeback. In the 54th minute, Enrique Barja produced a sensational right-footed volley following an assist from Raul Garcia to level the score. The momentum had firmly swung, and in the 62nd minute, the visitors were awarded a penalty after Javi Galan handled the ball in the box. Substitute Ante Budimir stepped up in the 64th minute and coolly converted the spot-kick, sending Ionut Andrei Radu the wrong way to give Osasuna the lead. Late Drama and Goal-Line Heroics The closing stages were a frantic affair as Celta pushed for an equalizer. Miguel Roman and Hugo Alvarez swung in multiple corners, but the delivery lacked the precision to find a teammate. In the 9th minute of stoppage time, Osasuna almost added a third when Ante Budimir saw his shot cleared off the line by a desperate Sergio Carreira . Despite the late pressure, Osasuna held firm to secure a 2-1 victory, with Enrique Barja earning plaudits for a standout performance."
